{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MatchInfo","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MatchInfo\/MatchInfoProtocol-Implementations"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isPartialMatch","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib17MatchInfoProtocolPAAE09isPartialB0Sbvp::SYNTHESIZED::s:4GLib9MatchInfoC","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"isPartialMatch","extendedModule":"GLib"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Usually if the string passed to g_regex_match*() matches as far as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"it goes, but is too short to match the entire pattern, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned. There are circumstances where it might be helpful to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"distinguish this case from other cases in which there is no match.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isPartialMatch"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Consider, for example, an application where a human is required to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type in data for a field with specific formatting requirements. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example might be a date in the form ddmmmyy, defined by the pattern"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"^\\d?\\d(jan|feb|mar|apr|may|jun|jul|aug|sep|oct|nov|dec)"},{"type":"text","text":"\\d\\d$”."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the application sees the user’s keystrokes one by one, and can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"check that what has been typed so far is potentially valid, it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"able to raise an error as soon as a mistake is made."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GRegex supports the concept of partial matching by means of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"partialSoft","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"partialHard","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" flags."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"When they are used, the return code for"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_regex_match()"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"g_regex_match_full()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is, as usual, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a complete match, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise. But, when these functions"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", you can check if the match was partial calling"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_match_info_is_partial_match()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The difference between ","type":"text"},{"code":"partialSoft","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"partialHard"},{"text":" is that when a partial match is encountered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"partialSoft"},{"type":"text","text":", matching continues to search for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"possible complete match, while with "},{"code":"partialHard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" matching","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"stops at the partial match.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"When both ","type":"text"},{"code":"partialSoft","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"partialHard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"are set, the latter takes precedence.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There were formerly some restrictions on the pattern for partial matching.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The restrictions no longer apply."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"code":"pcrepartial(3)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for more information on partial matching.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MatchInfo\/isPartialMatch"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/matchinfo\/ispartialmatch"]}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MatchInfo/isPartialMatch":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Usually if the string passed to g_regex_match*() matches as far as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it goes, but is too short to match the entire pattern, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. There are circumstances where it might be helpful to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"distinguish this case from other cases in which there is no match.","type":"text"}],"title":"isPartialMatch","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/matchinfo\/ispartialmatch","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MatchInfo\/isPartialMatch","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isPartialMatch","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MatchInfo/MatchInfoProtocol-Implementations":{"title":"MatchInfoProtocol Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/matchinfo\/matchinfoprotocol-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MatchInfo\/MatchInfoProtocol-Implementations","abstract":[],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MatchInfo":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MatchInfo"}],"title":"MatchInfo","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/matchinfo","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MatchInfo","abstract":[{"text":"A GMatchInfo is an opaque struct used to return information about","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"matches.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MatchInfo"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"}}}